## 2. Political context dataset

The dataset in `data/political_context/` (CSV files and the compiled values in `raw_data.py`) is licensed
under the [Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0)](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

You are free to share and adapt the material for any purpose, provided you give appropriate credit,
provide a link to the license and indicate if changes were made.

### Sources of the political context data

The dataset compiles publicly available election results and information on governments from:

- Amt für Statistik Berlin-Brandenburg / Landeswahlleiter Berlin and Brandenburg (official election reports)
- Die Bundeswahlleiterin (results of state elections)
- Landtag Brandenburg (parliamentary handbooks)
- wahlrecht.de, the election-data compilations of the Konrad-Adenauer-Stiftung, and Wikipedia

The source of every value is given in the `source` columns of the tables. Election results are official
statistics; the respective providers' terms of use apply to the original publications.

## 3. Legislation data (not included)

The analysis uses the preprocessed event logs of Hillmann, Fahrenkrog-Petersen and Mendling (2025),
<https://github.com/pjhi/coPM-German-State-Parliament-Data>, which are licensed under CC BY 4.0 by
their authors. They are not redistributed here. The logs are based on the documentation services
(*Parlamentsdokumentation*) of the state parliaments:

- Landtag von Baden-Württemberg – https://www.landtag-bw.de
- Abgeordnetenhaus Berlin – https://www.parlament-berlin.de
- Landtag Brandenburg – https://www.landtag.brandenburg.de

